 no failed services, new listeners, or package-health damage.","evidence_ids":["cmd-38cb5645475e4c9f","cmd-f1abbb5472ec43c5","cmd-b096b35e03fd47d2","cmd-c66bdbc11d074bfc","cmd-9df1cb2b58b540d5","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node2:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material backup outcomes are satisfied. The provider-wide restart protocol is also complete for both nodes: each has a healthy pre-restart observation, acknowledgement, changed boot identity corroborated by the fixed lifecycle snapshots, recovered services and configuration, and a successful post-restart end-to-end backup.","limitations":["No execution initiated by cron at 02:15 was captured; schedule timing is supported by the installed cron entry and active crond, while job behavior was verified through equivalent manual invocations.","The source directory was initially absent and was created empty, so the archive evidence validates transfer and restoration of an empty directory tree but does not exercise nonempty file-content fidelity.","The lifecycle temporary-file inventory covers /tmp rather than /var/tmp, so persistence of the explicitly created restart log files is inferred from the absence of any cleanup command rather than directly observed."]}
